From: SF2000 Linux port
Subject: mips: sf2000: provide the no-MMU fbdev mapping address

The no-MMU mmap core can only create a shared character-device mapping when
the file operation reports the device's actual address through
get_unmapped_area.  fbdev has a generic implementation for this exact case,
guarded by FB_PROVIDE_GET_FB_UNMAPPED_AREA, but the hidden option has to be
selected by a platform.

Select it for SF2000 whenever fbdev is enabled.  This lets ordinary fbdev
applications mmap the simple-framebuffer at 0x00f10000 instead of failing
with ENODEV after otherwise successful FBIOGET_* ioctls.

--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -262,6 +262,7 @@ config MIPS_SF2000
 	select CEVT_R4K
 	select CSRC_R4K
 	select DMA_NONCOHERENT
+	select FB_PROVIDE_GET_FB_UNMAPPED_AREA if FB
 	select IRQ_MIPS_CPU
 	select MIPS_GENERIC
 	select NO_EXCEPT_FILL
